# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D guide ended by mentioning that local encodings are needed when working with two dimensions. This guide takes that step, for the **two-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model on a square lattice**, using the **Verstraete-Cirac (VC) encoding** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"
msgstr "Nagtapos ang 1D na gabay sa pagbanggit na kailangan ang mga lokal na encoding kapag nagtatrabaho sa dalawang dimensyon. Ginagawa ng gabay na ito ang hakbang na iyon, para sa **dalawang-dimensyong Fermi-Hubbard model sa isang square lattice**, gamit ang **Verstraete-Cirac (VC) encoding** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are three differences from the 1D problem, forming the basis of this work:\n"
msgstr "May tatlong pagkakaiba mula sa 1D na problema, na bumubuo sa batayan ng gawaing ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The flow sets multiply.** A chain has two arrow orientations; a square lattice has four (east, west, north, south), and each is a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths (one per lattice row or column) rather than a single path.\n"
msgstr "**Dumarami ang mga flow set.** Ang isang chain ay may dalawang oryentasyon ng arrow; ang square lattice ay may apat (east, west, north, south), at ang bawat isa ay unyon ng mga vertex-disjoint na directed path (isa bawat row o column ng lattice) sa halip na iisang path.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoding gains an ancilla per site**, not one for the whole system, giving a\n"
msgstr "## **Nagkakaroon ang encoding ng ancilla bawat site**, hindi isa para sa buong sistema, na nagbibigay ng\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$. Transfer operators become weight-3 (horizontal) and weight-4 (vertical) Paulis, and each of the four flow sets maps to its own Pauli shape, so each needs its own diagonalizing Clifford.\n"
msgstr "    ratio ng qubit-sa-mode na $2$. Ang mga transfer operator ay nagiging weight-3 (pahalang) at weight-4 (patayo) na mga Pauli, at ang bawat isa sa apat na flow set ay minamapa sa sarili nitong hugis ng Pauli, kaya ang bawat isa ay nangangailangan ng sarili nitong diagonalizing na Clifford.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a subspace**: the joint $+1$\n"
msgstr "## **Tapat lang ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian sa isang subspace**: ang magkasamang $+1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    eigenspace of the plaquette constraints that every 2D local encoding carries <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). In 1D the encoding was a plain isometry and the verification was a spectrum check. Here, the comparison has to be projected, as [step 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers) illustrates.\n"
msgstr "    eigenspace ng mga plaquette constraint na dala ng bawat 2D na lokal na encoding <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). Sa 1D, ang encoding ay payak na isometry at ang pag-verify ay pagsusuri ng spectrum. Dito, kailangang i-project ang paghahambing, gaya ng inilalarawan ng [hakbang 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is the same shape as in 1D: the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step becomes constant in the lattice size, at $24$ ($16$ for the hopping, matching Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), plus $8$ for the interaction), while a term-by-term Trotterization of the same encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly. The gate count still grows with the number of bonds, of course; what becomes size-independent is how many layers those gates occupy. Depths throughout are counted on an abstract, fully connected register; mapping the encoding onto a device’s restricted coupling map is its own problem, which is discussed at the end.\n"
msgstr "Ang pakinabang ay kapareho ng hugis sa 1D: ang two-qubit depth ng isang hakbang ng Trotter ay nagiging pirmi sa laki ng lattice, sa $24$ ($16$ para sa hopping, tugma sa Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), dagdag ang $8$ para sa interaksyon), habang ang term-by-term na Trotterization ng parehong naka-encode na Hamiltonian ay linear na lumalaki. Lumalaki pa rin ang bilang ng Gate kasabay ng bilang ng mga bond, siyempre; ang nagiging hindi nakadepende sa laki ay kung ilang layer ang sinasakop ng mga Gate na iyon. Ang mga depth sa kabuuan ay binibilang sa isang abstract, ganap na konektadong register; ang pagmamapa ng encoding sa restricted na coupling map ng isang device ay sarili nitong problema, na tinatalakay sa dulo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The lattice and its four orientations {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"
msgstr "Ang lattice at ang apat na oryentasyon nito {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first change is visible on the directed interaction graph. Sites are numbered in row-major order, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, and every bond carries both orientations, as the chain did in 1D, but now the bonds run along two axes:\n"
msgstr "Ang unang pagbabago ay nakikita sa directed na interaction graph. Binibilang ang mga site ayon sa row-major na pagkakasunod, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, at ang bawat bond ay may parehong oryentasyon, gaya ng chain sa 1D, pero ngayon ang mga bond ay tumatakbo sa dalawang axis:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The commutation rule is the 1D one, unchanged: two transfer operators sharing a site **commute** when the arrows flow through it and **anticommute** when they clash. However, a site now has up to four incident bonds rather than two, so the arrows through it can clash in more ways, and a set of arrows that never clashes is no longer a single path. Reading the horizontal arrows left-to-right gives one such set, the vertical arrows from top-to-bottom gives another, and reversing each gives two more. These are the east, west, north, and south flow sets that organize everything that follows.\n"
msgstr "Ang commutation rule ay ang sa 1D, walang pagbabago: ang dalawang transfer operator na may iisang site ay **nagko-commute** kapag dumadaloy ang mga arrow sa pamamagitan nito at **nag-aanticommute** kapag nagbabanggaan. Gayunpaman, ang isang site ngayon ay may hanggang apat na incident na bond sa halip na dalawa, kaya ang mga arrow sa pamamagitan nito ay maaaring magbanggaan sa mas maraming paraan, at ang hanay ng mga arrow na hindi kailanman nagbabanggaan ay hindi na isang path lang. Ang pagbasa sa mga pahalang na arrow mula kaliwa pakanan ay nagbibigay ng isang ganoong set, ang mga patayong arrow mula itaas pababa ay isa pa, at ang pagbaliktad ng bawat isa ay nagbibigay ng dalawa pa. Ito ang mga east, west, north, at south na flow set na nag-oorganisa ng lahat ng susunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Verstraete-Cirac encoding {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"
msgstr "Ang Verstraete-Cirac encoding {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verstraete-Cirac (VC) pairs every fermionic mode $j$ with its own auxiliary qubit. With $N$ lattice sites, mode $j$ lives on qubit $j$ and its ancilla is on qubit $N + j$, so the register holds $2N$ qubits. Vertex operators stay as simple as they can be,\n"
msgstr "Ipinapares ng Verstraete-Cirac (VC) ang bawat fermionic na mode $j$ sa sarili nitong auxiliary na qubit. Sa $N$ na site ng lattice, ang mode $j$ ay nasa qubit $j$ at ang ancilla nito ay nasa qubit $N + j$, kaya ang register ay may $2N$ na qubit. Nananatiling kasimple hangga't maaari ang mga vertex operator,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what makes the occupations directly readable later. Transfer operators depend on the edge orientation. For a horizontal edge $j \\to k$ with $j$ the western site, and a vertical edge with $j$ the northern site,\n"
msgstr "na siyang nagpapadali sa direktang pagbasa ng mga occupation mamaya. Ang mga transfer operator ay nakadepende sa oryentasyon ng edge. Para sa pahalang na edge na $j \\to k$ kung saan ang $j$ ay ang kanlurang site, at isang patayong edge kung saan ang $j$ ay ang hilagang site,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "a weight-3 “triangle” and a weight-4 “square”. Identifying each arrow matters: with $j$ as the western site, $j \\to k$ points east, but with $j$ as the northern site, it points south. The reverse orientations follow from the identity $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which turns the `XXZ` triangle into `YYZ`, and the `XYXY` square into `YXXY`. Those four distinct labels are the four flow sets, and the rest of this guide tracks them.\n"
msgstr "isang weight-3 na “triangle” at isang weight-4 na “square”. Mahalaga ang pagtukoy sa bawat arrow: kapag ang $j$ ang kanlurang site, ang $j \\to k$ ay nakaturo sa east, pero kapag ang $j$ ang hilagang site, nakaturo ito sa south. Ang mga reverse na oryentasyon ay sumusunod sa identity na $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, na ginagawang `YYZ` ang triangle na `XXZ`, at `YXXY` ang square na `XYXY`. Ang apat na magkakaibang label na iyon ang apat na flow set, at ang natitirang bahagi ng gabay na ito ay sinusubaybayan ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **These are not quite Eq. (A1) of Ref.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), which states “up to single-qubit rotations” and differs in three ways worth naming, since a reader checking the paper will notice:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Hindi eksaktong ito ang Eq. (A1) ng Ref.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), na nagsasabing “hanggang sa single-qubit rotations” at may tatlong pagkakaiba na dapat banggitin, dahil mapapansin ito ng sinumang magsusuri sa paper:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The prefactor:** Eq. (A1) carries none. The $\\tfrac12$ here is what makes $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, matching the normalization $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ that [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") uses. The paper only ever needs its transfer operators inside $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, where a scale factor is absorbed into the rotation angle; here they have to be *operators* that satisfy an identity.\n"
msgstr "**Ang prefactor:** Walang taglay nito ang Eq. (A1). Ang $\\tfrac12$ dito ang nagpapatotoo na $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, na tugma sa normalization na $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ na ginagamit ng [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Ang kailangan lang ng paper sa mga transfer operator nito ay nasa loob ng $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, kung saan ang scale factor ay nasasama sa rotation angle; dito, kailangan silang maging *mga operator* na sumusunod sa isang identity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Orientation:** Eq. (A1) selects letters by the row parity of $j$, which for a horizontal edge is the same for both endpoints, so it does not distinguish $T_{jk}$ from $T_{kj}$. The paper recovers the orientation separately, by conjugating with a layer of $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. This guide instead folds it into the encoding, deriving the reverse from $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which is what makes the two orientations land on different Paulis in step 3.\n"
msgstr "**Ang orientation:** Pinipili ng Eq. (A1) ang mga letra ayon sa row parity ng $j$, na para sa horizontal na edge ay pareho sa dalawang dulo, kaya hindi nito nakikilala ang $T_{jk}$ sa $T_{kj}$. Hiwalay na binabawi ng paper ang orientation sa pamamagitan ng pag-conjugate gamit ang isang layer ng $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. Sa halip, isinasama ito ng gabay na ito sa encoding, at hinuhugot ang reverse mula sa $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, kaya napupunta ang dalawang orientation sa magkaibang Pauli sa step 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **The vertical shape:** Eq. (A1) alternates `XXXX` and `YYYY` by row parity, where this guide uses a single `XYXY`. These are two ways of getting the same thing: a letter asymmetry that makes a vertical edge clash correctly with the horizontal edges meeting it. Do not read the difference as a free basis choice. Dropping the parity alternation and using a single `XXXX` breaks the algebra outright, which is why the distinct letters are checked rather than assumed.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Ang vertical na hugis:** Pinapalitan ng Eq. (A1) ang `XXXX` at `YYYY` ayon sa row parity, samantalang ang gabay na ito ay gumagamit ng iisang `XYXY`. Dalawa itong paraan para sa iisang layunin: isang asymmetry ng mga letra na nagpapagawa sa vertical na edge na tamang mag-clash sa mga horizontal na edge na nagtatagpo rito. Huwag ituring na malayang pagpili ng basis ang pagkakaiba. Ang pag-alis ng parity alternation at paggamit ng iisang `XXXX` ay tuluyang sumisira sa algebra, kaya sinusuri ang magkakaibang letra sa halip na ipagpalagay lang.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The ancilla is attached to a *site*, giving the ratio $2$; it is the Derby-Klassen encoding that places an auxiliary qubit per (odd) plaquette, for the smaller ratio $3/2$. VC is used here because its transfer operators are the ones whose diagonalizing Cliffords Ref.   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives in closed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Nakakabit ang ancilla sa isang *site*, kaya ang ratio ay $2$; ang Derby-Klassen encoding naman ang naglalagay ng isang auxiliary qubit bawat (odd) plaquette, para sa mas maliit na ratio na $3/2$. Ginagamit dito ang VC dahil ang mga transfer operator nito ang may mga diagonalizing Clifford na ibinibigay ng Ref.   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) sa closed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian on a square lattice {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"
msgstr "1. Ang Hamiltonian sa isang square lattice {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The construction is the same as in 1D, but with a two-dimensional edge list. Sites keep the row-major numbering used for the figure above, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, so that horizontal bonds connect consecutive indices, and vertical bonds connect indices differing by `cols`:\n"
msgstr "Pareho ang konstruksyon sa 1D, pero may two-dimensional na edge list. Pinapanatili ng mga site ang row-major na pagnunumero na ginamit sa figure sa itaas, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, kaya ang mga horizontal na bond ay nag-uugnay ng magkakasunod na index, at ang mga vertical na bond ay nag-uugnay ng mga index na magkaiba ng `cols`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"four-flow-sets-instead-of-two\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Four flow sets instead of two {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"
msgstr "2. Apat na flow set sa halip na dalawa {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each hopping term is classified by the direction its arrow points on the lattice. Comparing the `divmod` row/column coordinates of the two endpoints separates horizontal from vertical edges, and the sign of the difference picks the orientation. Everything diagonal (the identity, the $V_j$ and the $V_j V_k$ terms) goes into a fifth group:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat hopping term ay inuuri ayon sa direksyong tinuturo ng arrow nito sa lattice. Ang paghahambing ng `divmod` na row/column coordinate ng dalawang dulo ang naghihiwalay sa horizontal at vertical na mga edge, at ang sign ng pagkakaiba ang pumipili ng orientation. Lahat ng diagonal (ang identity, ang $V_j$ at ang $V_j V_k$ na mga term) ay napupunta sa ikalimang grupo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Orientation convention.** The names are simply read off the figure above: an arrow is **east** or **west** as it points right or left along a row, and **north** or **south** as it points up or down a column. Since the numbering runs row-major, east and south are the index-increasing directions. Nothing downstream depends on the names (they only label groups), but they are easy to confuse, so it is worth fixing them against the picture. Ref.   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) names its square-lattice flow sets the same way.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Orientation convention.** Ang mga pangalan ay basta binasa mula sa figure sa itaas: ang arrow ay **east** o **west** depende kung nakaturo ito pakanan o pakaliwa sa isang row, at **north** o **south** depende kung nakaturo ito pataas o pababa sa isang column. Dahil row-major ang pagnunumero, ang east at south ang mga direksyong tumataas ang index. Walang nakadepende sa mga pangalan sa susunod na mga hakbang (mga label lang ito ng grupo), pero madaling malito ang mga ito, kaya mainam na iayon sa larawan. Pareho ang pagpapangalan ng Ref.   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) sa mga flow set nito sa square lattice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Within one flow set every arrow either meets another head-to-tail or does not meet it at all, as in 1D, so a flow set still commutes term-by-term and its evolution carries no Trotter error. What is new is that a flow set is now disconnected: the east set of a `rows x cols` lattice consists of `rows` independent left-to-right paths. That disconnection is a gift rather than a complication, as step 6 shows.\n"
msgstr "Sa loob ng isang flow set, bawat arrow ay alinman sa nagtatagpo ng ulo-sa-buntot sa isa pa o hindi talaga nagtatagpo, gaya sa 1D, kaya ang isang flow set ay nagko-commute pa rin term-by-term at walang Trotter error ang evolution nito. Ang bago ay hindi na konektado ang isang flow set: ang east set ng isang `rows x cols` na lattice ay binubuo ng `rows` na magkakahiwalay na landas na kaliwa-pakanan. Biyaya ang pagkakahiwalay na iyon at hindi komplikasyon, gaya ng ipapakita ng step 6.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"encode-the-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encode the operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"
msgstr "3. I-encode ang operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is one function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string, which is handed to [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Compared with the 1D version, the body has more cases: diagonal, horizontal, vertical, and the reverse orientations through $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"
msgstr "Ang encoding ay isang function na nagmamapa ng isang generalized transfer operator sa isang Pauli string, na ipinapasa sa [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Kumpara sa 1D na bersyon, mas maraming kaso ang katawan nito: diagonal, horizontal, vertical, at ang mga reverse orientation sa pamamagitan ng $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one problem. [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") calls back with a generator and nothing else, while deciding a bond’s Pauli string also needs `cols` to recover row and column coordinates from a mode index. Rather than nest the functions to close over it, [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial) binds it, which keeps both functions at the top level and independently callable.\n"
msgstr "May isang problema. Ang [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") ay tumatawag pabalik gamit ang isang generator lang at wala nang iba, samantalang ang pagpapasya sa Pauli string ng isang bond ay nangangailangan din ng `cols` para makuha ang row at column coordinate mula sa isang mode index. Sa halip na i-nest ang mga function para i-close over ito, binibigkis ito ng [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial), kaya nananatili ang dalawang function sa top level at maaaring tawagin nang hiwalay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The point of grouping before mapping can be seen immediately: each flow set encodes to a single Pauli shape, uniform across the whole set.\n"
msgstr "Makikita agad ang silbi ng pag-grupo bago mag-map: ang bawat flow set ay nag-e-encode sa iisang Pauli shape, pare-pareho sa buong set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping shapes are distinct, so each flow set gets its own Clifford in [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). The reverse orientations are different Paulis, not the same ones relabeled; this is why a 2D flow-set synthesis needs four circuits, where the 1D synthesis needs one.\n"
msgstr "Magkakaiba ang apat na hopping shape, kaya ang bawat flow set ay may sariling Clifford sa [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). Ang mga reverse orientation ay magkakaibang Pauli, hindi ang parehong Pauli na nilagyan lang ng bagong label; kaya ang 2D na flow-set synthesis ay nangangailangan ng apat na circuit, samantalang isa lang ang kailangan ng 1D na synthesis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Transpile with the custom encoding {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "4. I-transpile gamit ang custom na encoding {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This stage is the 1D one with a wider qubit register: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") maps the $N$-mode register onto $2N$ qubits, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") carries the encoding, and its `product_formula` argument selects how the resulting [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) is decomposed. Compare [step 6 of the 1D guide](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), which builds the same pipeline for a single ancilla.\n"
msgstr "Ang yugtong ito ay ang 1D na bersyon na may mas malapad na qubit register: minamapa ng [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") ang $N$-mode na register sa $2N$ na qubit, dala ng [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") ang encoding, at pinipili ng `product_formula` argument nito kung paano idi-decompose ang nagreresultang [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). Ihambing ang [step 6 ng 1D na gabay](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), na bumubuo ng parehong pipeline para sa iisang ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Five gates, carrying the 6, 6, 6, 6, and 22 terms counted in step 2. Each is mapped and synthesized independently, so the partition decided at the fermionic level survives all the way into the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Limang Gate, na may 6, 6, 6, 6, at 22 na term na binilang sa step 2. Bawat isa ay minamapa at sini-synthesize nang hiwalay, kaya ang partition na napagpasyahan sa fermionic na antas ay nananatili hanggang sa circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the baseline: the encoding and the grouping are both in place, but [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) synthesizes each flow set term by term, and the depth grows with the lattice.\n"
msgstr "Iyan ang baseline: nakalagay na ang encoding at ang pag-grupo, pero sini-synthesize ng [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ang bawat flow set term by term, at lumalaki ang depth kasabay ng lattice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. A depth-2 Clifford per flow set {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"
msgstr "5. Isang depth-2 na Clifford bawat flow set {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mechanism is the same as in 1D: conjugate a whole commuting flow set by a Clifford that maps each of its terms to a distinct weight-1 Pauli, so that the evolution of the entire set costs only single-qubit rotations. In 1D, one brickwork of `CZ` gates did this.\n"
msgstr "Pareho ang mekanismo sa 1D: i-conjugate ang buong commuting na flow set gamit ang isang Clifford na nagmamapa sa bawat term nito sa isang natatanging weight-1 na Pauli, kaya ang evolution ng buong set ay nagkakahalaga lang ng single-qubit rotations. Sa 1D, isang brickwork ng `CZ` na mga gate ang gumawa nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In 2D, each flow set needs its own circuit, following Section IV C and Fig. 7 of Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). All four act on one line of the lattice at a time (a row for east/west, a column for north/south) together with that line’s ancillas, and all four have the same three-part shape:\n"
msgstr "Sa 2D, ang bawat flow set ay nangangailangan ng sariling circuit, ayon sa Section IV C at Fig. 7 ng Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). Lahat ng apat ay kumikilos sa isang linya ng lattice sa bawat pagkakataon (isang row para sa east/west, isang column para sa north/south) kasama ang mga ancilla ng linyang iyon, at lahat ng apat ay may parehong tatlong-bahaging hugis:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A layer of single-qubit rotations, putting each qubit in the basis its flow set needs.\n"
msgstr "Isang layer ng single-qubit rotations, na naglalagay sa bawat qubit sa basis na kailangan ng flow set nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A first `CX` layer, always site-to-ancilla on the same site.\n"
msgstr "Isang unang `CX` layer, laging site-papuntang-ancilla sa parehong site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A second `CX` layer, coupling neighbors along the line.\n"
msgstr "Isang pangalawang `CX` layer, na nag-uugnay ng mga magkakapitbahay sa kahabaan ng linya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2 and 3 are the only two-qubit layers, so the two-qubit depth is $2$, regardless of how long the line is. They are written out one function per flow set below. The rotations are what they are because they were found, by conjugating each flow set’s terms and requiring distinct weight-1 images, so treat them as given and rely on the check that follows.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga step 2 at 3 lang ang dalawang two-qubit layer, kaya ang two-qubit depth ay $2$, gaano man kahaba ang linya. Isinulat ang mga ito nang isang function bawat flow set sa ibaba. Ang mga rotation ay ganoon dahil natuklasan ang mga ito, sa pamamagitan ng pag-conjugate sa mga term ng bawat flow set at pag-require ng natatanging weight-1 na mga imahe, kaya ituring silang ibinigay at umasa sa pagsusuring kasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two horizontal sets are the simplest. Their terms are weight-3, `XXZ` and `YYZ`, and differ only by the extra $S$ that turns $X$ into $Y$ on the sites:\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang horizontal na set ang pinakasimple. Weight-3 ang mga term nila, `XXZ` at `YYZ`, at nagkakaiba lang sa dagdag na $S$ na nagpapalit ng $X$ sa $Y$ sa mga site:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two vertical sets are weight-4, `XYXY` and `YXXY`, and are correspondingly busier: the rotations alternate with the position along the line, and the second `CX` layer alternates too, coupling sites on even positions and ancillas on odd ones (or the reverse):\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang vertical na set ay weight-4, `XYXY` at `YXXY`, at mas abala nang naaayon: nag-aalternate ang mga rotation ayon sa posisyon sa kahabaan ng linya, at nag-aalternate din ang pangalawang `CX` layer, na nag-uugnay ng mga site sa even na posisyon at ng mga ancilla sa odd na posisyon (o kabaligtaran):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drawn on a single three-site line (its sites first, then their ancillas) the whole mechanism fits in one picture. The triangle shape is the clearer of the two: a basis change on the ancillas, then two `CX` layers, the first pairs each site with its own ancilla and the second reaches to the next site along the line.\n"
msgstr "Kapag iginuhit sa isang linyang may tatlong site (mga site muna, saka ang mga ancilla nila), magkakasya ang buong mekanismo sa isang larawan. Ang triangle na hugis ang mas malinaw sa dalawa: isang basis change sa mga ancilla, saka dalawang `CX` layer, kung saan ang una ay nagpapares sa bawat site sa sarili nitong ancilla at ang pangalawa ay umaabot sa susunod na site sa linya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The square shape needs more single-qubit work (the rotations alternate along the line) and its second `CX` layer alternates between coupling sites and coupling ancillas:\n"
msgstr "Ang square na hugis ay nangangailangan ng mas maraming single-qubit na gawain (nag-aalternate ang mga rotation sa linya) at ang pangalawang `CX` layer nito ay nag-aalternate sa pag-uugnay ng mga site at pag-uugnay ng mga ancilla:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are two `CX` layers deep, and adding sites to the line widens them without deepening them; that is the whole constant-depth claim, visible by inspection. The west and north Cliffords differ only in their single-qubit layers, so they are not drawn separately.\n"
msgstr "Parehong dalawang `CX` layer ang lalim ng dalawa, at ang pagdagdag ng mga site sa linya ay nagpapalapad sa mga ito nang hindi pinalalalim; iyan ang buong constant-depth na pahayag, nakikita sa simpleng pagsisiyasat. Ang west at north na mga Clifford ay nagkakaiba lang sa kanilang single-qubit na mga layer, kaya hindi na sila iginuhit nang hiwalay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the synthesis still needs is determining where each term ends up. A line of $L$ sites carries $L - 1$ bonds, each contributing one term, so the helper below returns one entry per bond: the qubit that the term landed on, and the single-qubit Pauli it became. Crucially, these are read off the conjugation rather than predicted. Unlike 1D, where one `CZ` brickwork maps $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ in closed form, there is no such formula here, and the ancillas of a column line are not contiguous. The only thing that differs between the flow sets is the Pauli string going in, which step 3 already printed:\n"
msgstr "Ang kailangan pa ng synthesis ay alamin kung saan napupunta ang bawat term. Ang isang linya ng $L$ na site ay may $L - 1$ na bond, bawat isa ay may isang term, kaya ang helper sa ibaba ay nagbabalik ng isang entry bawat bond: ang qubit kung saan lumapag ang term, at ang single-qubit na Pauli na naging ito. Mahalaga, binabasa ang mga ito mula sa conjugation sa halip na hinuhulaan. Hindi tulad ng 1D, kung saan ang isang `CZ` brickwork ay nagmamapa ng $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ sa closed form, walang ganoong formula dito, at ang mga ancilla ng isang column line ay hindi magkakadikit. Ang tanging nagkakaiba sa pagitan ng mga flow set ay ang Pauli string na pumapasok, na naipakita na ng step 3:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The images must come out distinct and weight-1, so that each term can be rotated independently on its own qubit; the two-qubit depth of $2$ is already visible in the four constructions above, each emitting two `CX` layers irrespective of the line length. Below, both properties are checked across every flow set, every line, and several lattice sizes. Step 6 then calls `clifford_supports`, so it is a working part of the synthesis rather than only a demonstration.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga imahe ay dapat lumabas na natatangi at weight-1, para ang bawat term ay maaaring i-rotate nang hiwalay sa sarili nitong qubit; ang two-qubit depth na $2$ ay kita na sa apat na konstruksyon sa itaas, bawat isa ay naglalabas ng dalawang `CX` layer anuman ang haba ng linya. Sa ibaba, sinusuri ang dalawang katangian sa bawat flow set, bawat linya, at ilang laki ng lattice. Pagkatapos, tatawagin ng Step 6 ang `clifford_supports`, kaya ito ay gumaganang bahagi ng synthesis at hindi lang demonstrasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Flow-set-aware synthesis {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "6. Flow-set-aware na synthesis {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The synthesis gets a helpful head start. Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself group by group, `synthesize` is called once per flow set (five times here, four hopping sets plus the diagonal group) so every hopping term it sees shares one Pauli shape, and one Clifford diagonalizes all of them. It only has to read that shape off the first term and sort the rest by which line they sit on. Then comes the observation that makes two dimensions cheaper than one might fear:\n"
msgstr "May malaking pakinabang ang synthesis sa simula. Dahil hinahati ng [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ang sarili nito grupo por grupo, ang `synthesize` ay tinatawag nang isang beses bawat flow set (limang beses dito, apat na hopping set kasama ang diagonal na grupo) kaya ang bawat hopping term na nakikita nito ay may parehong Pauli shape, at isang Clifford ang nagda-diagonalize sa lahat. Kailangan lang nitong basahin ang hugis mula sa unang term at ayusin ang iba ayon sa linyang kinalalagyan nila. Saka ang obserbasyon na ginagawang mas mura ang dalawang dimensyon kaysa sa inaakala:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The components of a single flow set are vertex-disjoint: the west set’s rows share no qubits. So all of a flow set’s Cliffords can be emitted together and they share the same two two-qubit layers, rather than queueing up one row after another. A flow set therefore costs a fixed number of layers (two for the Clifford and two for its inverse) no matter how many rows or columns the lattice has, which is why the total depth ends up constant.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Ang mga bahagi ng isang flow set ay vertex-disjoint: walang pinagsasaluhang qubit ang mga row ng west set. Kaya lahat ng Clifford ng isang flow set ay maaaring ilabas nang sabay-sabay at pareho nilang ginagamit ang parehong dalawang two-qubit layer, sa halip na pumila nang isa-isa kada row. Kaya ang isang flow set ay nagkakahalaga ng takdang bilang ng layer (dalawa para sa Clifford at dalawa para sa inverse nito) gaano man karami ang row o column ng lattice, kaya nagiging constant ang kabuuang depth.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in 1D, this is deliberately written for this encoding: it recognizes the four Pauli shapes and raises on anything else rather than falling back silently. It also assumes the one-flow-set-per-gate split above, and says so; more than one hopping shape in a single gate means the grouping was not applied, which is an error rather than something to work around.\n"
msgstr "Gaya sa 1D, sadyang isinulat ito para sa encoding na ito: kinikilala nito ang apat na Pauli shape at nagtataas ng error sa anupamang iba sa halip na tahimik na bumalik sa iba. Ipinapalagay din nito ang hati ng isang-flow-set-bawat-gate sa itaas, at sinasabi ito; ang higit sa isang hopping shape sa iisang gate ay nangangahulugang hindi nailapat ang pag-grupo, na isang error at hindi bagay na iwasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Like its 1D counterpart, this synthesis takes no number of Trotter steps. A Trotter step has to cycle *between* the flow sets, but `transpile_trotter_step` below decomposes the fermionic circuit into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per set, so this method only ever sees one set at a time and could only repeat *within* it, which changes nothing: repeating one operator just splits its own evolution into equal pieces.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tulad ng 1D na katapat nito, walang bilang ng Trotter step ang synthesis na ito. Ang isang Trotter step ay kailangang umikot *sa pagitan* ng mga flow set, pero dini-decompose ng `transpile_trotter_step` sa ibaba ang fermionic na circuit sa isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") na gate bawat set, kaya isang set lang ang nakikita ng method na ito sa bawat pagkakataon at maaari lang itong umulit *sa loob* nito, na walang binabago: ang pag-ulit ng isang operator ay hahatiin lang ang sarili nitong evolution sa pantay na mga piraso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Multi-step Trotterization therefore needs a product formula that respects the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") inside a single gate, before the decomposition. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that, and [step 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) uses it to measure the convergence.\n"
msgstr "  Kaya ang multi-step na Trotterization ay nangangailangan ng product formula na iginagalang ang [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") ng operator sa loob ng iisang gate, bago ang decomposition. Ginagawa iyon ng [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), at ginagamit ito ng [step 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) para sukatin ang convergence.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Note the two similarly named classes at play. Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter), used as the baseline above, acts on the *mapped* Hamiltonian, where the grouping is already gone. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the fermionic counterpart, and it is the one that can still see the flow sets.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pansinin ang dalawang magkahawig na pangalan ng klase na narito. Ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ng Qiskit, na ginamit bilang baseline sa itaas, ay kumikilos sa *namapang* Hamiltonian, kung saan wala na ang pag-grupo. Ang [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ang fermionic na katapat nito, at ito ang nakakakita pa rin sa mga flow set.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-result-constant-depth\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. The result: constant depth {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"
msgstr "7. Ang resulta: constant na depth {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything so far ran on the single $3 \\times 3$ lattice built in step 1. Comparing the two synthesis paths across growing lattices needs that whole sequence (operator, grouping, encoding, circuit, pass manager) repeated per size, so it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Lahat ng nauna ay tumakbo sa iisang $3 \\times 3$ na lattice na binuo sa step 1. Ang paghahambing ng dalawang synthesis path sa lumalaking mga lattice ay nangangailangan ng buong sekwensiyang iyon (operator, pag-grupo, encoding, circuit, pass manager) na ulitin bawat laki, kaya sulit na i-wrap ito nang isang beses:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collecting both metrics across a range of lattice sizes and plotting them against the lattice edge makes the difference plain:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagkolekta ng parehong sukatan sa isang saklaw ng mga laki ng lattice at pag-plot ng mga ito laban sa gilid ng lattice ay nagpapalinaw ng pagkakaiba:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit depth is 24 and constant from $3 \\times 3$ to $8 \\times 8$ (that is 18 qubits up to 128), while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) applied to the identically encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly with the lattice edge, from 47 to 92. The gate count grows under both, since there are $O(N)$ terms to apply either way; what the flow sets remove is the growth in how many layers those gates occupy.\n"
msgstr "Ang two-qubit depth ay 24 at constant mula $3 \\times 3$ hanggang $8 \\times 8$ (iyon ay 18 qubit hanggang 128), samantalang ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) na inilapat sa magkaparehong naka-encode na Hamiltonian ay lumalaki nang linear kasabay ng gilid ng lattice, mula 47 hanggang 92. Lumalaki ang gate count sa dalawa, dahil may $O(N)$ na term na ilalapat sa alinmang paraan; ang inaalis ng mga flow set ay ang paglaki ng bilang ng layer na sinasakop ng mga gate na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The budget splits into 16 for the hopping and eight for the interaction:\n"
msgstr "Ang budget ay nahahati sa 16 para sa hopping at walo para sa interaction:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each of the four flow sets costs $2 + 2$ two-qubit layers: its Clifford going in and the inverse coming out, both depth two by construction, with only single-qubit rotations in between. That is $4 \\times 4 = 16$, which is the figure Ref. <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) quotes, since it counts the hopping terms only. Setting $U = 0$ in the code above reproduces it.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat isa sa apat na flow set ay nagkakahalaga ng $2 + 2$ na two-qubit layer: ang Clifford nito papasok at ang inverse palabas, parehong depth dalawa ayon sa konstruksyon, na may single-qubit rotations lang sa pagitan. Iyon ay $4 \\times 4 = 16$, na siyang bilang na binabanggit ng Ref. <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), dahil mga hopping term lang ang binibilang nito. Ang pagtatakda ng $U = 0$ sa code sa itaas ay nagpapalabas nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagonal group adds the remaining eight. Its `Rzz` gates pack into four layers, and each `Rzz` decomposes into two `CX` gates around a single-qubit rotation, so $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Four layers is optimal: on a square lattice, the interaction reaches only nearest neighbors, so every interior site carries four `Rzz` gates (one per bond) and can take part in only one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Ang diagonal na grupo ang nagdadagdag ng natitirang walo. Ang mga `Rzz` na gate nito ay nagkakasya sa apat na layer, at bawat `Rzz` ay nagde-decompose sa dalawang `CX` na gate sa paligid ng isang single-qubit rotation, kaya $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Optimal ang apat na layer: sa isang square lattice, ang interaction ay umaabot lang sa pinakamalapit na kapitbahay, kaya bawat interior na site ay may apat na `Rzz` na gate (isa bawat bond) at isa lang ang maaari nitong salihan sa isang pagkakataon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing in either sum refers to the lattice size, which is the whole point.\n"
msgstr "Walang binabanggit ang alinmang kabuuan tungkol sa laki ng lattice, na siyang buong punto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Verify the circuit {#8-verify-the-circuit}"
msgstr "8. I-verify ang circuit {#8-verify-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The flow-set synthesis and [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) describe the same Trotter step of the same encoded Hamiltonian, so their unitaries must agree up to a global phase. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Ang flow-set synthesis at ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ay naglalarawan ng parehong Trotter step ng parehong naka-encode na Hamiltonian, kaya dapat magkatugma ang mga unitary nila hanggang sa global phase. Mas mura ang mga random statevector sa pagtuklas ng anumang hindi pagkakatugma kaysa sa pagbuo ng buong unitary:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both circuits are decomposed down to one- and two-qubit gates *before* being applied to a state. Left un-decomposed, each high-level `Evolution` instruction forces [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) to build its full $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$ dense operator; decomposing first lets it apply gates one at a time instead, which is several hundred times faster here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Parehong dini-decompose ang dalawang circuit pababa sa one- at two-qubit na mga gate *bago* ilapat sa isang state. Kapag hindi dini-decompose, ang bawat high-level na `Evolution` na instruction ay pipilit sa [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) na buuin ang buong $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$ na dense operator nito; ang pag-decompose muna ay nagpapahintulot dito na ilapat ang mga gate nang isa-isa, na ilang daang beses na mas mabilis dito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the same phase across several random states is what closes the gap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Parehong mahalaga ang dalawang kalahati ng pagsusuring iyon. Ang unit-modulus na overlap sa isang state ay kailangan pero hindi sapat: ang synthesis na nagkamali sa state-dependent na phase ay makikita pa rin ito. Ang pag-require ng parehong phase sa ilang random na state ang nagsasara ng puwang.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-stabilizers\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Verify the physics on the stabilizer subspace {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"
msgstr "9. I-verify ang physics sa stabilizer subspace {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the two-dimensional wrinkle. In 1D, the encoding was an isometry, and comparing spectra against a Jordan-Wigner reference was enough. VC is not an isometry: it uses $2N$ qubits for $N$ modes, so a $2^{2N}$-dimensional space holds a $2^N$-dimensional physical one. This is generic to local encodings in two dimensions (the surplus qubits are constrained by local commuting symmetries, one per plaquette <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) and it means the encoded Hamiltonian represents the fermionic one faithfully only on the joint $+1$ eigenspace of those constraints.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang kulubot ng dalawang dimensyon. Sa 1D, isometry ang encoding, at sapat na ang paghahambing ng mga spectrum laban sa Jordan-Wigner na reference. Hindi isometry ang VC: gumagamit ito ng $2N$ na qubit para sa $N$ na mode, kaya ang $2^{2N}$-dimensional na espasyo ay naglalaman ng $2^N$-dimensional na pisikal. Karaniwan ito sa mga local encoding sa dalawang dimensyon (ang sobrang mga qubit ay nilimitahan ng mga local commuting na symmetry, isa bawat plaquette <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) at nangangahulugan itong ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian ay kumakatawan lang nang tapat sa fermionic sa magkasanib na $+1$ eigenspace ng mga constraint na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The word **stabilizer** does double duty in this subject, and the two meanings are unrelated. Ref.   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) uses it for the commuting transfer operators of a flow set, which form a stabilizer group that the Cliffords of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) diagonalize (a compilation device, and the sense meant everywhere above). This section uses it in the error-correction sense: operators whose $+1$ eigenspace is the physical subspace. Ref.   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) explicitly flags this collision and sets the second meaning aside; the plaquette constraints below are a property of the VC encoding   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), not a result of the flow-set framework.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Babala\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Ang salitang **stabilizer** ay may dalawang gamit sa paksang ito, at hindi magkaugnay ang dalawang kahulugan. Ginagamit ito ng Ref.   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) para sa mga commuting na transfer operator ng isang flow set, na bumubuo ng stabilizer group na dina-diagonalize ng mga Clifford ng [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) (isang compilation device, at ang kahulugang ginamit sa lahat ng nasa itaas). Ginagamit ito ng seksyong ito sa kahulugang error-correction: mga operator na ang $+1$ eigenspace ang pisikal na subspace. Tahasang binabanggit ng Ref.   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) ang banggaan na ito at isinasantabi ang pangalawang kahulugan; ang mga plaquette constraint sa ibaba ay katangian ng VC encoding   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), hindi resulta ng flow-set framework.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The generators are constructed here rather than quoted: one per square face, and each is simply the encoded **edge**-operator loop around that face.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga generator ay binuo dito sa halip na sipiin: isa bawat square na mukha, at bawat isa ay ang naka-encode na **edge**-operator loop sa paligid ng mukhang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edge operators are the natural object for this. A closed loop of them is a symmetry of any particle-number-conserving Hamiltonian, whereas the corresponding loop of transfer operators is not: the two differ by a vertex operator on each bond’s source site,\n"
msgstr "Ang mga edge operator ang natural na bagay para rito. Ang saradong loop ng mga ito ay symmetry ng anumang Hamiltonian na nagpapanatili ng bilang ng particle, samantalang ang katumbas na loop ng mga transfer operator ay hindi: nagkakaiba ang dalawa ng isang vertex operator sa source site ng bawat bond,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Around a closed loop every site is the source of exactly one bond, so the loop collects one $V_j$ per site, which is the **local parity** of the plaquette’s four sites. That local parity is what makes the difference: the Hamiltonian hops particles across the plaquette boundary, so it conserves only the *global* parity. The bare transfer loop therefore fails to commute with it, while the edge loop (which carries the parity factor) commutes.\n"
msgstr "Sa paligid ng saradong loop, bawat site ay source ng eksaktong isang bond, kaya ang loop ay nangongolekta ng isang $V_j$ bawat site, na siyang **local parity** ng apat na site ng plaquette. Ang local parity na iyon ang gumagawa ng pagkakaiba: ang Hamiltonian ay nagha-hop ng mga particle sa hangganan ng plaquette, kaya *global* parity lang ang pinapanatili nito. Kaya ang hubad na transfer loop ay hindi nagko-commute rito, habang ang edge loop (na may parity factor) ay nagko-commute.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since the encoding is defined on transfer operators, mapping an edge operator needs the relation above. That is a five-line callback, and it slots into [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") exactly as `vc_action` slots into [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang encoding ay nakadefine sa mga transfer operator, ang pagmamapa ng isang edge operator ay nangangailangan ng relasyon sa itaas. Isa itong limang-linyang callback, at pumapasok ito sa [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") nang eksakto kung paano pumapasok ang `vc_action` sa [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each generator has weight $6$, spread over two of its plaquette’s physical qubits and four ancillas. They are involutory and commute with the encoded Hamiltonian, so the physical subspace is preserved by the dynamics. Both properties are statements about operators, so they are checked symbolically on the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) algebra, no $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$ matrices required:\n"
msgstr "Bawat generator ay may weight na $6$, nakakalat sa dalawa sa mga pisikal na qubit ng plaquette nito at apat na ancilla. Involutory ang mga ito at nagko-commute sa naka-encode na Hamiltonian, kaya napapanatili ng dynamics ang pisikal na subspace. Pareho itong mga pahayag tungkol sa mga operator, kaya sinusuri ang mga ito nang symbolic sa [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) na algebra, walang kailangang $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$ na matrix:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the stabilizers in hand, the comparison needs no basis correspondence, because $V_j = Z_j$ means the occupations live on the same physical qubits in both pictures. So: write a product state directly on the physical qubits with the ancillas in $|0\\rangle$, project it onto the stabilizer subspace, evolve with the encoded Hamiltonian, and read the site densities $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ off both sides.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nasa kamay na ang mga stabilizer, hindi na kailangan ng basis correspondence ang paghahambing, dahil ang $V_j = Z_j$ ay nangangahulugang nasa parehong pisikal na qubit ang mga occupation sa dalawang larawan. Kaya: sumulat ng product state nang direkta sa mga pisikal na qubit na may mga ancilla sa $|0\\rangle$, i-project ito sa stabilizer subspace, i-evolve gamit ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian, at basahin ang mga site density na $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ sa magkabilang panig.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every step here stays at the level of a vector. The projector is applied one $(1 + S)/2$ factor at a time instead of being multiplied out, and the time evolution uses [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), which computes $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ without ever forming $e^{-iHt}$. Since the encoded Hamiltonian is a sparse $2^{2N}$-dimensional operator, that distinction is what keeps this section cheap.\n"
msgstr "Bawat hakbang dito ay nananatili sa antas ng vector. Inilalapat ang projector nang isang $(1 + S)/2$ na factor bawat pagkakataon sa halip na i-multiply out, at ang time evolution ay gumagamit ng [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), na kumukuwenta ng $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ nang hindi binubuo ang $e^{-iHt}$. Dahil ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian ay sparse na $2^{2N}$-dimensional na operator, ang pagkakaibang iyon ang nagpapanatiling mura sa seksyong ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those are the encoded densities; they match the Jordan-Wigner reference to machine precision, on a lattice whose encoding is faithful only after projection.\n"
msgstr "Iyan ang mga naka-encode na density; tugma ang mga ito sa Jordan-Wigner na reference hanggang machine precision, sa isang lattice na ang encoding ay tapat lang pagkatapos ng projection.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"measure-the-trotter-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "10. Measure the Trotter convergence {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"
msgstr "10. Sukatin ang Trotter convergence {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Step 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) established that the two syntheses agree with each other, which is a statement about equivalence rather than accuracy: both describe the same single Trotter step, so both carry the same Trotter error. Measuring that error needs an exact reference, and step 9 just built one.\n"
msgstr "Itinatag ng [Step 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) na magkatugma ang dalawang synthesis, na pahayag tungkol sa pagkakapareho at hindi sa katumpakan: parehong inilalarawan ng dalawa ang iisang Trotter step, kaya pareho ang Trotter error nila. Ang pagsukat sa error na iyon ay nangangailangan ng eksaktong reference, at nakabuo na ng isa ang step 9.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The step count comes from [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), the fermionic counterpart of the qubit-level formula used as the baseline earlier. Applied to the whole grouped operator before the decomposition, its repetition cycles between the four flow sets and the diagonal group instead of within any one of them:\n"
msgstr "Ang bilang ng step ay galing sa [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), ang fermionic na katapat ng qubit-level na formula na ginamit bilang baseline kanina. Kapag inilapat sa buong naka-grupong operator bago ang decomposition, ang pag-ulit nito ay umiikot sa pagitan ng apat na flow set at ng diagonal na grupo sa halip na sa loob ng alinman sa mga iyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fidelity climbs monotonically toward one as the steps shorten, which is the behavior a product formula must show. Shortening the steps is only one of the two knobs; [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") trades them against each other at a higher order, as [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) measures.\n"
msgstr "Umaakyat nang monotonic ang fidelity papunta sa isa habang umiikli ang mga step, na siyang dapat ipakita ng isang product formula. Ang pagpapaikli ng mga step ay isa lang sa dalawang knob; ang [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") ay nagpapalitan ng mga ito sa mas mataas na order, gaya ng sinusukat ng [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single step of this Hamiltonian at $t = 1$ is a poor approximation (the four hopping sets and the interaction do not commute) so the first row is far from one, and that is the point: the convergence is what confirms the construction, not any single row.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang step ng Hamiltonian na ito sa $t = 1$ ay mahinang approximation (hindi nagko-commute ang apat na hopping set at ang interaction) kaya malayo sa isa ang unang row, at iyon ang punto: ang convergence ang nagpapatunay sa konstruksyon, hindi ang anumang isang row.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor of the schedule spans every mode of this lattice, so narrowing a factor to its support is a no-op here and the absolute qubit indices `FlowSetSynthesis` matches on are unchanged. A synthesis written for an operator whose groups touch only part of the register would have to account for that relabeling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang bawat factor ng schedule ay sumasaklaw sa bawat mode ng lattice na ito, kaya ang pagpapakitid ng isang factor sa support nito ay walang epekto dito at hindi nagbabago ang absolute na mga qubit index na tinutugma ng `FlowSetSynthesis`. Ang synthesis na isinulat para sa operator na ang mga grupo ay humahawak lang sa bahagi ng register ay kailangang isaalang-alang ang relabeling na iyon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Mga dapat tandaan {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two dimensions changes the bookkeeping, not the recipe.** Every ingredient from the 1D guide carries over unmodified: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") for the grouping, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for the mismatched register, and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") to wire it into the transpiler. What grew is the number of cases inside each.\n"
msgstr "**Binabago ng dalawang dimensyon ang bookkeeping, hindi ang recipe.** Bawat sangkap mula sa 1D na gabay ay dinadala nang walang pagbabago: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") para sa pag-grupo, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") para sa encoding, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") para sa hindi magkatugmang register, at [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") para ikabit ito sa transpiler. Ang lumaki ay ang bilang ng mga kaso sa loob ng bawat isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Disjointness is what makes 2D constant-depth.** A flow set decomposes into vertex-disjoint lines, so its Cliffords are emitted in parallel and share two two-qubit layers no matter how large the lattice is. Four flow sets and a diagonal group then give a fixed budget: here $16$ for the four flow sets plus $8$ for the diagonal interaction group.\n"
msgstr "**Ang disjointness ang nagpapa-constant-depth sa 2D.** Ang isang flow set ay nagde-decompose sa vertex-disjoint na mga linya, kaya ang mga Clifford nito ay inilalabas nang parallel at pinagsasaluhan ang dalawang two-qubit layer gaano man kalaki ang lattice. Ang apat na flow set at isang diagonal na grupo ay nagbibigay ng takdang budget: dito ay $16$ para sa apat na flow set kasama ang $8$ para sa diagonal na interaction group.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Each orientation is its own Pauli shape.** $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ turns `XXZ` into `YYZ` and `XYXY` into `YXXY`, so the four flow sets need four Cliffords. Assuming that one Clifford covers both orientations of an axis is the easiest way to get a 2D flow-set synthesis wrong.\n"
msgstr "**Bawat orientation ay sariling Pauli shape.** Ang $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ ay ginagawang `YYZ` ang `XXZ` at `YXXY` ang `XYXY`, kaya ang apat na flow set ay nangangailangan ng apat na Clifford. Ang pag-aakalang isang Clifford ang sumasaklaw sa dalawang orientation ng isang axis ang pinakamadaling paraan para magkamali sa 2D na flow-set synthesis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Read supports off the conjugation.** In 1D, one `CZ` brickwork gives the images in closed form. In 2D there is no such formula, and column lines have non-contiguous ancillas, so a hand-derived guess at where each term lands is fragile. Conjugating and inspecting the result costs one [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) construction and cannot be wrong; it also means an equally valid Clifford that lands the terms elsewhere keeps working.\n"
msgstr "**Basahin ang mga support mula sa conjugation.** Sa 1D, ang isang `CZ` brickwork ay nagbibigay ng mga imahe sa closed form. Sa 2D, walang ganoong formula, at ang mga column line ay may hindi magkakadikit na ancilla, kaya marupok ang hand-derived na hula kung saan lalapag ang bawat term. Ang pag-conjugate at pagsisiyasat sa resulta ay nagkakahalaga ng isang [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) na konstruksyon at hindi maaaring magkamali; nangangahulugan din ito na ang isang katumbas na validong Clifford na naglalapag ng mga term sa ibang lugar ay patuloy na gumagana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Let the grouping do the sorting.** Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself per group, the synthesis is handed one flow set at a time and never has to re-derive the partition: it reads one Pauli shape off the first term and picks the matching Clifford. Assuming that, and raising when it does not hold, is what keeps `synthesize` short.\n"
msgstr "**Hayaang ang pag-grupo ang mag-ayos.** Dahil hinahati ng [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ang sarili nito kada grupo, ang synthesis ay binibigyan ng isang flow set sa bawat pagkakataon at hindi na kailangang kuwentahin muli ang partition: binabasa nito ang isang Pauli shape mula sa unang term at pinipili ang katugmang Clifford. Ang pag-aakalang iyon, at ang pagtataas ng error kapag hindi ito totoo, ang nagpapanatiling maikli sa `synthesize`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The step count sits above the split.** The synthesis here sees one flow set per gate, so it cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that in fermionic space, before the decomposition, which is what makes a convergence test possible at all.\n"
msgstr "**Nasa itaas ng hati ang bilang ng step.** Ang synthesis dito ay nakakakita ng isang flow set bawat gate, kaya hindi nito mahahati ang evolution sa mga set. Ginagawa iyon ng [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") sa fermionic space, bago ang decomposition, na siyang nagpapaging-posible sa convergence test.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify on the subspace.** A $2N$-qubit encoding of $N$ modes is faithful only where the stabilizers say it is. Because VC keeps $V_j = Z_j$, the cheapest reliable check is to project a product state and compare densities: no intertwiner and no spectral matching, which is unreliable when the restricted Hamiltonian is degenerate.\n"
msgstr "**I-verify sa subspace.** Ang $2N$-qubit na encoding ng $N$ mode ay tapat lamang kung saan sinasabi ng mga stabilizer na ito ay tapat. Dahil pinapanatili ng VC ang $V_j = Z_j$, ang pinakamurang maaasahang pagsusuri ay i-project ang isang product state at ihambing ang mga density: walang intertwiner at walang spectral matching, na hindi maaasahan kapag degenerate ang restricted na Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The encoded Hamiltonian commutes with the stabilizers, so the projection only has to be applied to the initial state. The evolution preserves the subspace by itself. On real hardware this is also what makes the encoding useful as an error-detection resource: the stabilizers can be measured.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Paalala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Nagko-commute ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian sa mga stabilizer, kaya ang projection ay kailangan lang ilapat sa paunang state. Ang evolution mismo ang nagpapanatili sa subspace. Sa totoong hardware, ito rin ang nagpapagamit sa encoding bilang resource sa error-detection: maaaring sukatin ang mga stabilizer.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next {#next}"
msgstr "Susunod {#next}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend what is above, and both are changes of ingredient rather than of method. The first is the encoding: Verstraete-Cirac was chosen here because Ref. <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives its diagonalizing Cliffords in closed form, but Derby-Klassen spends one ancilla per odd plaquette instead of one per site, for a qubit-to-mode ratio of $3/2$ rather than $2$. Its transfer operators have different Pauli shapes, so a port amounts to rewriting the encoding function of [step 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) and finding the Clifford for each new shape; the grouping, the layout, and the synthesis scaffolding carry over untouched.\n"
msgstr "Dalawang direksyon ang nagpapalawak sa nasa itaas, at parehong pagbabago ng sangkap at hindi ng paraan. Ang una ay ang encoding: pinili dito ang Verstraete-Cirac dahil ibinibigay ng Ref. <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) ang mga diagonalizing Clifford nito sa closed form, pero gumagastos ang Derby-Klassen ng isang ancilla bawat odd na plaquette sa halip na isa bawat site, para sa qubit-to-mode ratio na $3/2$ sa halip na $2$. Magkakaiba ang Pauli shape ng mga transfer operator nito, kaya ang pag-port ay nangangahulugan ng pagsulat muli ng encoding function ng [step 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) at paghahanap ng Clifford para sa bawat bagong shape; ang pag-grupo, ang layout, at ang synthesis scaffolding ay dinadala nang walang pagbabago.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second is the lattice itself. Everything here assumes open boundaries and a single fermionic species. Periodic boundaries close each line into a cycle: the arrows still all commute, since each meets the next head-to-tail, but the two Clifford shapes of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) are built for a line with endpoints. A cycle of $L$ sites carries $L$ bonds per orientation where a line carries $L - 1$, so the wrap-around bond has no place in the construction and needs handling of its own. A spinful model is easier: it doubles the register and adds on-site interaction terms to the diagonal group, without touching the flow sets. Neither disturbs the constant-depth argument, but both change the bookkeeping, which, as the first takeaway says, is the part that two dimensions makes bigger.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangalawa ay ang lattice mismo. Ipinapalagay ng lahat dito ang open na mga hangganan at isang uri lang ng fermion. Ang periodic na mga hangganan ay nagsasara sa bawat linya bilang cycle: nagko-commute pa rin ang lahat ng arrow, dahil bawat isa ay nagtatagpo sa susunod ng ulo-sa-buntot, pero ang dalawang Clifford shape ng [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) ay ginawa para sa linyang may mga dulo. Ang cycle ng $L$ na site ay may $L$ na bond bawat orientation samantalang ang linya ay may $L - 1$, kaya walang lugar ang wrap-around na bond sa konstruksyon at nangangailangan ng sariling pagtrato. Mas madali ang spinful na modelo: dinodoble nito ang register at nagdaragdag ng on-site na interaction term sa diagonal na grupo, nang hindi ginagalaw ang mga flow set. Walang nakakagambala sa constant-depth na argumento, pero parehong binabago ang bookkeeping, na, gaya ng sinasabi ng unang takeaway, ay ang bahaging pinalalaki ng dalawang dimensyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Hardware connectivity is not addressed here.** Every circuit above is built on an abstract register where any pair of qubits can interact, and the reported depths are counted in that setting. Real devices have a restricted coupling map, and mapping this encoding onto one is a substantial problem in its own right: the VC register is a $2N$-qubit graph whose gates run between a site and its own ancilla, between neighboring sites and between neighboring ancillas, so a layout has to keep all three kinds of pairs adjacent simultaneously. If it cannot, the transpiler inserts `SWAP` gates, and the layers they add are what the constant-depth construction was buying back. Ref.   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) likewise quotes its depth figure under an assumed square connectivity graph with `CX` as the only native entangler. Finding good layouts and routing strategies for local encodings on a given device topology is beyond this guide’s scope.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Hindi tinutugunan dito ang hardware connectivity.** Bawat circuit sa itaas ay binuo sa abstract na register kung saan anumang pares ng qubit ay maaaring mag-interact, at ang mga iniulat na depth ay binibilang sa ganoong setting. Ang totoong mga device ay may limitadong coupling map, at ang pagmamapa ng encoding na ito sa isa ay malaking problema sa sarili nito: ang VC register ay isang $2N$-qubit na graph na ang mga gate ay tumatakbo sa pagitan ng isang site at sarili nitong ancilla, sa pagitan ng magkakapitbahay na site at sa pagitan ng magkakapitbahay na ancilla, kaya ang isang layout ay kailangang panatilihing magkatabi ang lahat ng tatlong uri ng pares nang sabay. Kung hindi, nagsisingit ang transpiler ng mga `SWAP` na gate, at ang mga layer na idinaragdag ng mga ito ang binabawi ng constant-depth na konstruksyon. Binabanggit din ng Ref.   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) ang depth figure nito sa ilalim ng ipinapalagay na square connectivity graph na `CX` lang ang native na entangler. Ang paghahanap ng mahusay na mga layout at routing strategy para sa mga local encoding sa isang partikular na device topology ay lampas sa saklaw ng gabay na ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

